					<tbody><tr>
						<td>
						<!-- #BeginEditable "PageBody" -->
						<h2><font size=3D"3" color=3D"#000000">
						<span style=3D"font-weight: 400">4. Taking Action</span></font></h2>
						<p>
						<font size=3D"2">Achieve Planner supports two main styles=20
						of work: structured work using project blocks to guide=20
						your work, and unstructured work where you plan as you=20
						go and select the best task to work on next from various=20
						alternatives.</font></p>
						<p>
						<font size=3D"2"><b>Structured Work Style</b></font></p>
						<p>
						<font size=3D"2">In the structured work style, project blocks serve a=
s your=20
						main plan for=20
						the day.</font></p>
						<p>
						<font size=3D"2">When it is time to work on a=20
						project block, you simply go to the prioritized task=20
						list for the project in the <b>Tasks</b> tab and start working your t=
asks=20
						in priority order.</font></p>
						<p>
						<font size=3D"2">You can filter the Tasks tab to only show=20
						you the tasks for your current project without getting=20
						distracted by anything else.</font></p>
						<p>
						<font size=3D"2">In this example, the Tasks tab is=20
						filtered to only view tasks for the 'Project Proposal=20
						for new joint product' project.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"center">
						<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/screenshots19=
/TasksTabFiltered.png" width=3D"519" height=3D"379"></p>
						<p>
						<font size=3D"2">You can easily switch to a different=20
						project using the project selector dropdown button...</font></p>
						<p align=3D"center">
						<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/screenshots19=
/TasksProjectSelectorDropdown.png" width=3D"446" height=3D"71"></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">Or you can use the <b>Actions=20
						-&gt; Switch Project</b> menu command (Ctrl+H) which will open=20
						a <b>Project Chooser</b> dialog where you can select the=20
						project you want to focus on.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"center">
						<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/screenshots19=
/ProjectChooserDialog.png" width=3D"424" height=3D"537"></p>
						<p>
						&nbsp;</p>
						<p>
						<font size=3D"2"><b>Project Blocks In Your Schedule Are=20
						Linked to Projects</b></font></p>
						<p>
						<font size=3D"2">You can also jump to the task list from=20
						the weekly schedule by right-clicking on a project block=20
						and selecting View Tasks from the context menu. This will take you in=
to the Tasks tab filtered by=20
						that project.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"center">
						<font size=3D"2">&nbsp;<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.co=
m/achieve/screenshots19/ViewTasksContext.png" width=3D"301" height=3D"65"><=
/font></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">Since Project Blocks act like regular=20
						appointments, the reminders window will pop up when it's=20
						time to start a new project block...</font></p>
						<p align=3D"center">
						<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/screenshots19=
/RemindersWindowSS.png" width=3D"504" height=3D"352"></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">And you can click on the <b>View Tasks</b>=20
						button to take you to the Tasks tab already filtered by=20
						that project.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">You just keep doing this throughout the day=20
						to get your most important work done.</font></p>
						<p>
						<font size=3D"2">Video Tutorial (link opens in new=20
						window):</font></p>
						<ul>
							<li><font size=3D"2">
							<a href=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/tour/GMDT-AP-Lesson5-T1-Do=
Step.htm">Working on Tasks</a>=20
- How to work on the tasks of a specific project</font></li>
						</ul>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2"><b><a name=3D"NextActionReminders">'Next Action' Rem=
inders</a> or Bookmarks</b></font></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">If you=20
						don=92t finish a task before you need to do something else, it is sti=
ll there in your task list=20
						ready to start again the next time you want to work on=20
						that project.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">You can even add a "next action" reminder task=20
						so you can easily remember where you left=20
						off (like a bookmark in a book.)</font></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">Here's what a next action reminder looks=20
						like...</font></p>
						<p align=3D"center">
						<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/screenshots19=
/NextActionReminderExample.png" width=3D"481" height=3D"84"></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">That way, when you start your project=20
						again, you know exactly where you left off and what you=20
						need to do next.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">Creating these next action reminders is=20
						very easy... You simply use the <b>Actions -&gt; Record=20
						Work/Expenses</b> menu item to indicate that you didn't=20
						complete the task just yet...</font></p>
						<p align=3D"center">
						<font size=3D"2">
						<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/screenshots19=
/WorkExpenseRecordSS.png" width=3D"480" height=3D"337"></font></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">And enter the next action remember as the=20
						follow up action.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">Video Tutorials (links open in new=20
						window):</font></p>
						<ul>
							<li><font size=3D"2">
							<a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/tour/GMD=
T-AP-Lesson5-T2-CompletingTasks.htm">Completing Tasks</a> - How to complete=
 tasks=20
in Achieve Planner</font></li>
							<li><font size=3D"2">
							<a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/tour/GMD=
T-AP-Lesson5-T3-NextActionReminders.htm">Next Action Reminders</a> - How to=
 'bookmark' tasks using next action=20
reminders</font></li>
						</ul>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<b>Unstructured Working Style</b></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">Achieve Planner is very flexible and also=20
						supports an 'unstructured' style of work, where you plan as you go=20
						and select the best task to work on next across all your=20
						projects.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">The Outline tab supports filtering your=20
						outline to only show the next actions available in each=20
						project.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"center">
						<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/screenshots19=
/OutlineNextActionsOnly.png" width=3D"235" height=3D"74"></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2"><b>Powerful Filtering</b></font></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">Achieve Planner has powerful filtering=20
						support to help you find the best tasks to work on next.=20
						You can use the funnel icon in the column header to=20
						filter the values in that column.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"center">
						<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/screenshots19=
/ColumnFilters.png" width=3D"225" height=3D"207"></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">Once you've setup the filter conditions=20
						you want, you can save a snapshot of the filters using=20
						the 'View/Filters' panel at the top-left edge of the=20
						main screen.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"center">
						<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/screenshots19=
/SavedFilterSnapshot.png" width=3D"196" height=3D"307"></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">Click on the 'New Filter' button to=20
						create a new filter snapshot of the current filter=20
						conditions.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">Video Tutorial (link opens in new=20
						window):</font></p>
						<ul>
							<li><font size=3D"2">
							<a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/tour/GMD=
T-AP-Lesson5-T4-FiltersOverview.htm">Filters</a> - How to use filters in Ac=
hieve Planner to=20
filter the grids</font></li>
						</ul>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2"><b>Contexts</b></font></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">Contexts are a useful way to tag related=20
						tasks across projects. For example, you could tag tasks=20
						based on location (home vs. work), type of activity=20
						(phone), or simply to tag them for easier filtering=20
						(Errand, Todo or Urgent.)</font></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">You can then use filtering to help you=20
						find your tagged tasks quickly and easily.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<b>Task Chooser Tab</b></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">The task chooser (<b>Go -&gt; Task Chooser</b>=20
						menu item) displays a sorted and=20
						filtered list of tasks across all your projects ranked using configur=
able=20
						criteria like priority and deadlines.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"center">
						<a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/screensho=
ts19/TaskChooserSS.png">
						<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/screenshots19=
/TaskChooserSS-TN.png" width=3D"520" height=3D"322"></a><br>
						<font size=3D"1">Click Image to View Larger Size</font></p>
						<p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">The Task Chooser even allows you to=20
						create a custom prioritized daily to-do list that is=20
						independent of the Outline structure.</font></p>
						<table border=3D"0" width=3D"100%" cellspacing=3D"0" cellpadding=3D"0=
" id=3D"table2">
							<tbody><tr>
								<td>
								<a href=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/tour/plan-your-work.htm">
								<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/images/PreviousPage=
.png" width=3D"130" height=3D"22" alt=3D"Previous Page"></a></td>
								<td>
								<p align=3D"center">
						<a href=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/download.php">
						<img border=3D"0" id=3D"img7" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/images/do=
